message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Unsafe or potentially unsafe advice from patient-facing large language model chatbots in bench evaluations of primary-care question sets: a systematic review and meta-analysis"
authors:
  - family-names: "Malikian"
    given-names: "Raphael"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-4326-4205"
    email: "rtmalikian@gmail.com"
date-released: 2026-11-13
version: "1.0.0"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rtmalikian/llm-chatbot-unsafe-advice-primary-care-meta-analysis"
abstract: "Cochrane-level systematic review and meta-analysis of unsafe or potentially unsafe responses from patient-facing LLM chatbots in bench evaluations of primary-care question sets: 95 model arms, 23 studies, 552 of 4,868 rated responses in the studies' worst safety tiers; pooled 10.5% (95% CI 9.3 to 11.9); GRADE very low."
keywords:
  - large language models
  - chatbots
  - patient safety
  - primary care
  - systematic review
  - meta-analysis
